statement:
Call a string *good* when every letter that appears in it appears the same number of times. Starting from the lowercase string `s`, you may apply these operations as often as you like, and each application counts as one operation:

- remove one character;
- add one lowercase character anywhere;
- turn one character into the letter right after it in the alphabet (`'a'` becomes `'b'`, and so on). There is no wrap-around: a `'z'` cannot be turned into `'a'`.

Return the fewest operations needed to make `s` good.

validator:
function validate([s]) {
  if (s.length < 3 || s.length > 20000) return 's must have 3 to 20,000 characters.';
  if (!/^[a-z]+$/.test(s)) return 's may contain only lowercase English letters.';
  return null;
}

